course: dictionary
lesson: 15604
title: Tamer: gentle, milder, or a trainer
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tame means gentle and used to people, not wild. Tamer is the comparing form: it means more tame than something else. «The kitten is tamer than the wolf» tells you the kitten is gentler.
explain: A tamer can also be a person. A lion tamer trains wild animals. Look at the clues: if the sentence mentions a circus, a whip or a ring, tamer is probably a person. If it compares two things, tamer is probably the comparing word.
explain: Tamer can describe a ride, a joke or a film that is less wild or less exciting. «The second ride was tamer than the first» means the second ride was milder. Always ask: is the sentence about a person, or about comparing two things? The clues will show you which meaning fits.
fact: A tamer is a person who tames or trains wild animals.
fact: «Tamer» is the comparing form of «tame»: more gentle and used to people.
fact: «Tamer» can also mean milder or less exciting, as in «a tamer joke».
fact: Many countries now ban wild animals in circuses, so you may read about lion tamers in old stories and history books.
fact: In a famous science experiment, foxes became tamer over many generations.
exercise: «The lion tamer stood in the ring with her whip.» What is a tamer? | *A person who tames or trains wild animals | A ticket seller at the circus | A big tent with flags on top | A wild animal that runs very fast
exercise: «The second ride was tamer than the first.» What does tamer mean here? | *Milder and less exciting | Taller and wider | Wetter and colder | Faster and louder
exercise: Which word in «Our hamster is tamer than our rabbit» means more gentle and used to people? | *tamer | hamster | our | rabbit
test: «This joke is tamer than the last one, so Mum laughed less.» What does tamer mean here? | *Milder and less rude | Longer and harder to follow | Sadder and slower | Funnier and louder
test: Which person would be called a tamer? | *A woman who trains lions for a circus | A man who sells popcorn at the circus | A girl who rides the big wheel | A boy who cleans the seats
exam: Lily says tamer always means wilder. Is she right? | Yes, tamer means louder and faster | *No, tamer means more gentle, or milder, the opposite of wilder | No, tamer is only a name for a circus | Yes, tamer means wilder and more dangerous
